# ==============================================================================
# Node 18 (languages/node/Dockerfile.alpine) — ACCEPTED RESIDUAL RISK
#
# Scope: node:18-alpine ONLY. Node 20/22/24/26 images are not affected.
# Root cause: dependencies vendored inside the npm CLI itself
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules), shipped by the final npm@10
# release (npm 10.9.9). The npm@10 line receives no further updates and npm 11+
# requires Node >= 20, so these findings are UNFIXABLE while Node 18 remains in
# matrix.json — Node 18 has been EOL upstream since 2025-04-30.
#
# Affected vendored packages / findings:
#   brace-expansion 2.0.2          -> CVE-2026-13149, CVE-2026-14257, CVE-2026-69152
#   ip-address 10.1.0              -> CVE-2026-69192
#   pacote 19.0.2 / 20.0.1         -> CVE-2026-9496 (2 findings)
#   picomatch 4.0.3                -> CVE-2026-33671
#   sigstore 3.1.0                 -> CVE-2026-48815
# (4 MEDIUM + 1 LOW findings remain visible — below the CRITICAL/HIGH gate.)
#
# RE-REVIEW: remove these entries as soon as Node 18 is dropped from
# matrix.json, or if npm@10 ever publishes a release with patched deps.
# ==============================================================================
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-9496
CVE-2026-33671
CVE-2026-48815

# ==============================================================================
# Go 1.25 (languages/go/Dockerfile.alpine) — ACCEPTED RESIDUAL RISK
#
# Scope: go:1.25-alpine ONLY. Go 1.26 and 1.27 images are not affected.
# Root cause: Go stdlib CVEs are only backported to the two latest Go releases
# (1.26 and 1.27). Go 1.25 is EOL upstream.
# Affected stdlib CVEs:
#   CVE-2026-78667  -> net/http Range headers DoS
#   CVE-2026-78669  -> net/http/internal/http2 excessive SETTINGS frames DoS
#   CVE-2026-97031  -> crypto/tls ECH outer extension references DoS
# ==============================================================================
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031
CVE-2026-111943

# ==============================================================================
# npm CLI Vendored Dependencies (languages/node, frameworks/nextjs, frameworks/nestjs)
#
# Scope: node:20/22/24/26-alpine and derived framework images.
# Root cause: dependencies vendored inside the npm CLI itself
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/minimatch/node_modules/brace-expansion
# and /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/node-gyp/node_modules/undici).
# These packages are build tooling shipped by upstream npm@12.2.0, not runtime application
# dependencies. Upstream npm has not yet released versions bumping these vendored deps.
# ==============================================================================
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-19534
CVE-2026-93748
CVE-2026-109869
CVE-2026-109383
CVE-2026-87018

# ==============================================================================
# Debian Bookworm / Trixie OS Packages — ACCEPTED RESIDUAL RISK (UNFIXABLE)
#
# Scope: Debian 12 (bookworm) / Debian 13 (trixie) container images.
# Root cause: Upstream Debian Security Tracker has marked these findings with
# no available patch/backport (Fixed Version: None). Standard apt-get upgrade
# is executed in all Dockerfiles but cannot resolve unpatched upstream packages.
#
# Findings:
#   CVE-2026-53613  -> util-linux mount TOCTOU
#   CVE-2026-76642  -> util-linux X-mount post-hooks
#   CVE-2026-78408  -> util-linux nsenter root cgroup migration
#   CVE-2026-78409  -> util-linux X-mount.subdir detached-tree symlink escape
#   CVE-2026-78410  -> util-linux restricted bind mounts owner/group/mode redirection
#   CVE-2026-12064  -> curl schemeless URL SSH host verification bypass
# ==============================================================================
